t or result persistence. Only the five existing non-sensitive preference keys are written.\n- Retains 1.1–1.3 task cancellation, strict JSON/raw-header AGV1 authentication, isolated migration, Base64 modes, exact input semantics and Android resource budgets.\n\nValidation: **62 Android test methods**, **6 offline migration tests**, **783 actual frozen desktop comparisons**, lint **0 errors / 40 existing warnings**, APK build/version/signature checks passed. Includes real Preferences DataStore disk reads, unknown/type-anomalous values, corrupted protobuf and file read/write I/O with successful recovery and later edits. Physical-device acceptance is **NOT RUN**: no device connected. Local JVM/filesystem evidence does not replace Android device evidence.\n\n中文：修复设置读取与恢复 #10，读取和编辑共用安全解码。合法设置保留，损坏存储重置为保护默认值；读取 I/O 保留最后有效值并重试，写入失败明确提示。中英恢复提示独立于操作消息，在当前进程内保留至确认。首次设置加载期间启用屏幕保护，加载前离开应用会清空敏感输入；不持久化输入、口令或明文。\n\nNo file functionality or UI redesign added. [Validation](https://github.com/Qrzzzz/AegisVaultMobile/blob/v1.4/docs/validation-1.4.md) · [Settings recovery contract and exact defaults](https://github.com/Qrzzzz/AegisVaultMobile/blob/v1.4/docs/settings-1.4.md). Recovery notice status itself is not persisted across process death; repaired protective preferences are persisted. Device lifecycle/clipboard/accessibility/process-restart acceptance remains pending, including issue #5's device gate.\n"}